<title>SINGAPORE: Inabata sells Meiban shares.</title>
<headline>Inabata sells Meiban shares.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inabata Singapore (Pte) Ltd has sold 2.1 million shares -- 2.43 percent of the issued share capital -- in Meiban Plastic Ltd, Meiban said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Meiban, a plastic injection moulded articles maker, said in a statement that Inabata sold the shares for Singapore S$0.73 each, lowering its holdings to 4.63 percent from 7.06 percent.</p>
<p>Inabata is wholly owned by Japan's Inabata &amp; Co Ltd, a trading house which specialises in chemicals and plastics.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
